OL,3,AChemistry Nobel awarded for solving
OL,4,Amystery of life's asymmetry
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Nobel Prize in Chemistry has been
OL,7,Fawarded to French scientist Henri B.
OL,8,FKagan and Japan's Kenso Soai for
OL,9,Fproviding a solution to the chemical
OL,10,Fmystery of life's asymmetry.
OL,12,FThe researchers discovered how nature
OL,13,Fexclusively makes the correct version
OL,14,Fof a molecule - rather than its mirror
OL,15,Fimage.
OL,17,FFor example, amino acid molecules, the
OL,18,Fbuilding blocks of proteins, exist as
OL,19,Ftwo forms that are each other's mirror
OL,20,Fimage.
OL,23,APub: 07-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,0,100
